// Title: Renamed MegaSync Execution
// Sigma ID: 643bdcac-8b82-49f4-9fd9-25a90b929f3b
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Sittikorn S
// Date: 2021-06-22 | Modified: 2023-02-03
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects the execution of a renamed MegaSync.exe as seen used by ransomware families like
//   Nefilim, Sodinokibi, Pysa, and Conti.
// False positives:
//   - Software that illegally integrates MegaSync in a renamed form
//   - Administrators that have renamed MegaSync
// References:
//   - https://redcanary.com/blog/rclone-mega-extortion/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_renamed_megasync.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "megasync.exe" and (not(FolderPath endswith "\\megasync.exe"))
